0..77 Comment "// A program sums two draws of two fair bits through `std.rand.Eff`, the host"
78..105 Comment "// interface of randomness."
106..108 Comment "//"
109..186 Comment "// Each `draw` names a width in bits, and the host replies an integer uniform"
187..262 Comment "// over `[0, 2^width)` from the entropy source of the operating system. The"
263..339 Comment "// sum of two draws of two bits lies from 0 to 6, and the program exits with"
340..346 Comment "// it."
347..349 Comment "//"
350..424 Comment "// `gandr run draws.gandr` exits with the sum and prints nothing. The same"
425..495 Comment "// `summed` runs under a handler of this source, a second model of the"
496..566 Comment "// interface that answers each draw from a fixed list. The corpus runs"
567..643 Comment "// `summed` under a third model, the exact one. It runs once for each of the"
644..718 Comment "// 16 sequences of answers, and each path weighs `2^-4`. Its `distributes`"
719..795 Comment "// states the weight of each sum: the count of pairs that give the sum, over"
796..802 Comment "// 16."
803..805 Comment "//"
806..880 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-evaluate/src/evaluate/rand.rs` — the host that"
881..937 Comment "//   serves the interface, and the exact model\'s answers"
938..1016 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-corpus/src/distribution.rs` — the runs summed into"
1017..1038 Comment "//   one distribution"
1039..1112 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-driver/tests/rand.rs` — the run and its range"
1114..1141 Comment "// The native finite lists."
